e wall-clock ceiling per arm, and what meta-test gap vs. EXPLICIT-MAML is acceptable for declaring the implicit arm \\\"successful\\\" (e.g., within 1 pp on classification, within 0.005 MSE on sine, ‖g‖ rel-error ≤ 1e-2 on the toy)? These thresholds belong in the final design.\\n4. **Tasks & data.** Are offline mirrors of MiniImageNet / CIFAR-FS / Omniglot available, or must I stay synthetic? My fallback is a synthetic Gaussian-mixture few-shot benchmark; if real-task data is available the classification arm should switch to it.\\n5. **Tier decision.** Should the deliverable specify Tier A (TorchOpt calls literally named, with API names marked as proposed-to-validate) or Tier B (functorch code that is fully specifiable without source access and is wrapped so a TorchOpt call can be slotted in once confirmed)?\\n\\n**B. Non-blocking defaults I will choose myself with stated rationale (overridable at approval time).**\\n- Inner optimizer = SGD with per-parameter LR (MetaSGD where available, plain SGD fallback).\\n- Damping λ swept over {0, 1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1} with 1e-2 as default (matches iMAML's reported regime).\\n- Neumann depth K = 5; CG iters T = 10 as defaults (typical neighboring-paper defaults).\\n- Meta-optimizer = Adam, β = 0.001 (standard).\\n- 3 seeds, meta-test set of 600 held-out tasks.\\n- All small enough for CPU (no GPU dependency in the design), since GPU is disabled.\\n- Gradient-fidelity metric on the toy uses the K=1 closed form; on other tasks it uses unrolled-K second-order as the reference.\\n- Synthetic Gaussian-mixture few-shot if no real dataset mirror is supplied.\\n\\n**C. Known gotchas I'll address in the final design (not blockers, listed for transparency).**\\n- `retain_graph=True` is required for the EXPLICIT arm; memory cost will be reported separately from grad-error so it doesn't contaminate the gradient-fidelity metric.\\n- For deeper inner loops, the Neumann series only converges if α · ‖H‖₂ < 1; I will verify this condition empirically before drawing conclusions about K.\\n- Truncated Neumann + CG are not the only options (there is also the Gauss–Newton/BFGS implicit-meta family); I include them only if there is room, as a sensitivity arm, *after* the primary five-arm comparison is locked in.\\n\\n**Status.** Awaiting researcher approval on (1)–(5) in section A before drafting the full design (rationale, controls, full hyperparameter table, analysis plan with statistical tests, and the concrete Tier-A vs. Tier-B implementation strategy). No experiment has been run; no outcomes are claimed.\\n\",\"evidence\":\"\\nEnvironment probe output (Python 3.12.3, Linux x86_64, 24 CPUs, ~707 GB free, no pip on PATH, no torch/torchopt/numpy/scipy, network disabled via curl https://pypi.org → \\\"Could not resolve host\\\", find / found no torchopt/torch dirs). /workspace/task.json content confirms a design-only scope; its embedded documents.track.md says \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" Scope notes saved to /workspace/notes/initial_inspection.md (46 lines) for the researcher's reference. No locally verified TorchOpt APIs: every TorchOpt symbol named in the plan is proposed-from-public-docs and explicitly flagged for researcher confirmation against the actual installed TorchOpt version.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Implicit gradient target is the inner-loop initialization θ₀ (iMAML setting), with MetaSGD-style per-parameter inner LR as a secondary arm.</item>\",\"$text\":\"First-order implicit (e.g., setting damping high or skipping the Gauss-Newton inversion) is acceptable as a within-arm condition; second-order implicit is the primary arm but not a hard requirement.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Default inner optimizer = SGD-with-per-parameter-LR (torchopt.MetaSGD candidate, torch.optim.SGD fallback); meta-optimizer = Adam, β = 0.001.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"No offline dataset mirrors of MiniImageNet / CIFAR-FS / Omniglot are present, so the classification arm will use a synthetic Gaussian-mixture N-way K-shot benchmark unless the researcher supplies data.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Compute is CPU-only with 24 cores and is feasible for the proposed small-network arms (MLP-40 / ConvNet-4-layer) within a multi-hour overnight budget; GPU is not used.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Tier B (functorch-based, TorchOpt-free) is a valid placeholder that maps 1-to-1 onto Tier A; swapping in the real TorchOpt call later is a single-file change behind a meta_solver.py interface.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"TorchOpt is NOT installed in this bubblewrap and cannot be installed (no pip, no network); therefore every TorchOpt API name in the plan is a public-docs-based proposal, not a locally verified fact.</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Minor: second-order vs. first-order implicit acceptability, Neumann depth default (5 vs. 10), CG iters default (10 vs. 20), damping λ default sweep grid, number of seeds (3 vs. 5).</item>\",\"$text\":\"BLOCKING: compute budget ceiling per arm and the empirical success thresholds (gap to EXPLICIT-MAML on acc/MSE, allowed ‖g_implicit − g_explicit‖ rel-error).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BLOCKING: which Tier (A: TorchOpt-literal, B: functorch-with-TorchOpt-slot) the researcher wants the deliverable to specify concretely.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BLOCKING: target of differentiation (initialization θ₀ vs. per-parameter inner LR vs. other meta-parameters).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BLOCKING: whether real few-shot datasets can be supplied offline, or whether the synthetic Gaussian-mixture benchmark is acceptable.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BLOCKING: which TorchOpt version / entry point is intended (MetaGradientModule, torchopt.diff.implicit_diff, MetaSGD, or Optax-style wrapper).</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-dbea72a9-46b2-46a4-a6dd-7e8ed7005301", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", 