ion 7 and the decision rule in section 9.\\n\\nIf the sanity run produces a gradient-relative-L2 greater than 1e-2 on the toy task or the alpha=0 sanity probe fails to return FOMAML, STOP and debug before launching the full sweep.\\n\\n## 13. What this design does not claim\\n\\n- No online benchmarks, no MiniImageNet or CIFAR-FS or Omniglot numbers.\\n- No fabricated empirical numbers of any kind. All quantitative statements are asymptotic or follow from algorithmic identity (for example O(params) vs O(params * K_inner) memory differential of the implicit-vs-explicit arms).\\n- No claim about TorchOpt behavior beyond what is publicly known about its differentiable meta-learning module. Any specific TorchOpt symbol named in this document carries the `assume v0.9-style:` tag and is to be validated against the installed version by the engineer.\\nPART5\\necho \\\"part5 done: $(wc -l < /workspace/notes/final_design.md) lines\\\"\\necho \\\"---\\\"\\nhead -5 /workspace/notes/final_design.md\\necho \\\"...\\\"\\ntail -5 /workspace/notes/final_design.md\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-fa3f81fd-8d79-45f8-9edf-37aa6ca35dfe", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 52}
